Source ocbuild's efibuild.sh from a pinned local copy, not from master.

Upstream's last act in build_oc.tool is to curl ocbuild's efibuild.sh off
the master branch and eval it. That is a mutable input executed at build
time: the script it fetches also decides which EDK II tree to clone, so
the whole build hangs off whatever master happened to say today.

This patch replaces the fetch with a read of $EFIBUILD_SH, which
internal/firmware's OpenCore build points at the checksum-verified copy
named in assets/pins/sources.tsv. The eval is kept exactly as upstream has it, so
efibuild.sh still runs in build_oc.tool's own shell and still sees the
positional parameters it expects -- the only thing that changes is where
the text comes from.

Applied by internal/firmware's OpenCore build with `git apply`, against
the tree unpacked from the pinned OpenCorePkg tarball.

--- a/build_oc.tool
+++ b/build_oc.tool
@@ -400,7 +400,11 @@
 export NO_ARCHIVES
 export DISCARD_SUBMODULES
 
-src=$(curl -LfsS https://raw.githubusercontent.com/acidanthera/ocbuild/master/efibuild.sh) && eval "$src" || exit 1
+if [ "${EFIBUILD_SH}" = "" ] || [ ! -f "${EFIBUILD_SH}" ]; then
+  echo "ERROR: EFIBUILD_SH must name a local, pinned copy of ocbuild efibuild.sh!"
+  exit 1
+fi
+src=$(cat "${EFIBUILD_SH}") && eval "$src" || exit 1
 
 cd Utilities/ocvalidate || exit 1
 ocv_tool=""
